<article class="env-definition" id="05RF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05RF">Definition <span data-tag="05RF">13.6.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a (pre-)triangulated category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $F : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{D}'$ be an exact functor. The <em>kernel of $F$</em> is the strictly full saturated (pre-)triangulated subcategory described in Lemma <a href="/tag/05RC" data-tag="05RC">13.6.2</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $H : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{A}$ be a homological functor. The <em>kernel of $H$</em> is the strictly full saturated (pre-)triangulated subcategory described in Lemma <a href="/tag/05RD" data-tag="05RD">13.6.3</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> These are sometimes denoted $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(F)$ or $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(H)$. </p>
</article>